21-40: Avoid using logger before logging.basicConfig to keep logging configuration effective

In the try/except ImportError block you call logger.warning before logging.basicConfig is invoked. When health/security import fails, that first log call will cause the logging module to create a default handler, and basicConfig later becomes a no-op. As a result, your intended file + stream configuration may never be applied in that scenario.

To keep logging consistent regardless of whether the health module is available, initialize logging before any logger is used, or replace the early warning with a plain print and move the health/security import block below the basicConfig section.

