229-245: Add functools.wraps and validate max_attempts parameter

The decorator needs two improvements:

Add @functools.wraps(func) on the wrapper to preserve the original function's metadata (__name__, __doc__, __wrapped__), which is the standard way to ensure decorators preserve wrapped function metadata.
Validate that max_attempts >= 1 at decorator initialization; otherwise last_exception remains None and raise None occurs.
Consider whether catching all Exception is intentional; a narrower set prevents hiding programming errors.
