244-257: Shutdown audit logging is valuable; watch for broad Exception masking

Emitting a BOT_SHUTDOWN audit entry with uptime and open positions is a solid addition. The broad except Exception ensures shutdown isn’t blocked by audit logging failures, which may be acceptable here.

If you want to distinguish between expected I/O problems and unexpected programming errors, you could narrow this except clause (e.g., to OSError) and let truly unexpected issues bubble up or at least be logged with logger.exception.

274-280: Use logger.exception() for better traceback capture on cleanup errors

The cleanup of self.health_runner via await self.health_runner.cleanup() is the documented way to stop an aiohttp server and perform graceful shutdown. To improve operational debugging, swap logger.warning for logger.exception to automatically capture the full traceback if cleanup fails:

