159-177: Use logging.exception() for better exception logging with automatic stack trace capture

Inside an except block, logging.exception() is the preferred approach over logging.error() when a stack trace is needed. It is equivalent to logging.error(..., exc_info=True) and will record the full stack trace for the currently handled exception.

Apply the suggested change:

        except Exception as e:
-            logger.error(f"❌ Scanner Start Fehler: {e}")
+            logger.exception("❌ Scanner Start Fehler")
